module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.comparison_keyed_on_part_of_the_identity_it_compares

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data comparison_keyed_on_part_of_the_identity_it_compares: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "comparison_keyed_on_part_of_the_identity_it_compares" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a comparison keys on a PROPER COMPONENT of the identity it is comparing, while both sides carry the whole one** (INVALID STATE: a decision over elements identified by a composite -- module path plus declaration name, path plus revision, host plus port, run id plus attempt -- reduces the deciding key to a component of that identity, and the discarded component is present, in scope, and used elsewhere in the same function. The decision may be a membership or equality test between two populations, or a LOOKUP over one; the shape of the decision is not the defect, the projection of the key is. HARM: two distinct elements that agree on the retained component are ONE key, so a member of one population is accepted as a member of the other by an element it is not. The wrong answer is per-element and silent: nothing is missing, nothing is unreached, and the diagnostic surface never fires. ",

    "Recognition rule: at the deciding line, is the key equal to the identity, or to a projection of it? The tell is that the DISCARDED component reappears a few lines later to RENDER the finding -- the code already knows the full identity and uses it for the message, having thrown it away for the decision. ",

    "NO ACCOUNTING EQUALITY DETECTS THIS, WHICH IS WHY IT NEEDS ITS OWN ROW. Denominator reconciliation -- checked == declared, checked + excluded == population, subject-narrowing checks of every kind -- verifies that every element was EXAMINED, and every one of them survives here, because the subject was complete and each element received an answer. The defect is in the ANSWER, not in the population, so the whole family of narrowing checks is structurally blind to it. Specimen gunbc#10496, measured across two arms in one dispatch over one corpus: every COUNT line was byte-identical between the correct key and the defective one, and only the discriminating control moved. ",

    "IT PRESENTS AS LATENT AND ITS LATENCY IS AN ACCIDENT, NOT A GUARD. The retained component is usually unique in the corpus that exists on the day it is written, so the defective key answers correctly for every element and the class ships green. Current-corpus uniqueness is not an enforced precondition and stops being true the week someone adds a row, so a repair justified by a collision census expires; the repair has to stand on the key being wrong. ",

    "THE DISCRIMINATING CONTROL IS THE COLLISION, AND NO ORDINARY CONTROL SUBSTITUTES FOR IT: two elements sharing the retained component, differing in the discarded one, with only one of them a member. A control that drops a member and expects it to be reported passes under both the correct and the defective key -- they agree whenever the retained component is unique -- so it proves the check runs and proves nothing about its key. Specimen gunbc#10503: the collision control refuses under the defective key by reporting NOTHING, which the join reads as ControlDidNotFire. ",

    "WHAT THE NEIGHBOURING ROWS DO NOT COVER, checked before this row was filed. check_subject_narrower_than_its_declared_claim is the opposite shape: there the subject is a strict subset of the claim, here the subject is complete and the verdict on a member is wrong. surface_shorthand_preempts_resolved_identity is the nearest neighbour and is genuinely adjacent -- deciding on a spelling where a resolved identity was available -- but its rule is CONSTRUCTION totality over a resolved binding and its trigger repairs evaluator value construction, which leaves a COMPARISON keyed on a component untouched. identity_absent_graph_traversal is the case where no identity is available to key on at all; here it was present on both sides and discarded. incidental_denominator_as_wall names the accidental-safety shape but its invalid state is a destructive operation guarded by an unrelated upstream filter, where this class has nothing guarding it -- the key itself is wrong. ",

    "Next-rung trigger, named as the capability rather than as an artifact: composite identities are carried as a TYPE whose equality is the identity, so a comparison cannot be written against one of its components -- at which point the key and the identity cannot differ and there is nothing for a control to discriminate. Until then this is review diligence plus a per-site collision control, which is mechanically preventable at best.)",

    "**A THIRD AXIS: CI EVIDENCE IDENTITY, WHERE THE COMPOSITE IS NOT A DECLARATION BUT A RUN** (calm-eagle-759 and bright-ram-778, 2026-09-05, filed here rather than as a new row because the mechanism is identical and only the subject differs). A verdict about a pull request was assembled by keying on `run_id`, when the identity of a set of job results is (run_id, ATTEMPT) -- a re-run KEEPS THE SAME RUN ID. One level up, the same reduction happens on the check-suite when the identity is (suite, EVENT), because a workflow_dispatch run emits the SAME job names as the pull_request run at the same head. Both times the discarded component was present and available, and both times it reappeared afterwards to EXPLAIN the result, which is this row's own tell. ",

    "THIS INSTANCE REPAIRED THIS ROW'S OWN INVALID STATE, AND IT IS A REPAIR RATHER THAN AN EXTENSION -- which is the distinction a reviewer should check. The three parts of this row did not agree with each other. The HARM sentence says two distinct elements that agree on the retained component are one key; the RECOGNITION RULE asks whether the key is equal to the identity or to a projection of it. Both are already general over ANY keyed decision. Only the invalid state said 'between two populations'. So the row already asserted the damage this instance exhibits, and its opening sentence had simply failed to admit the shape that produces it. The invalid state above is now written to what the harm sentence already covered -- comparison and lookup alike -- rather than enumerating a second admitted shape beside the first, which would invite another append the first time someone finds a keyed join or a keyed dedup. ",

    "THE FOUR NEIGHBOURS THIS ROW ARGUES AGAINST WERE RE-READ AT THE NEW WIDTH, because a widening can silently swallow a neighbour and merge two classes instead of repairing one. All four arguments still hold. check_subject_narrower_than_its_declared_claim is about POPULATION completeness and says nothing about the key, so widening the decision shape does not touch it. identity_absent_graph_traversal still turns on AVAILABILITY -- there no identity exists to key on, here it was present and discarded. incidental_denominator_as_wall still turns on an unrelated upstream filter supplying accidental safety, where this class has nothing guarding it. surface_shorthand_preempts_resolved_identity is the one worth stating precisely, because it is nearest and the gap narrows: there the key is a SURFACE SPELLING standing in for a resolved binding, which is a different REPRESENTATION of the identity, not a COMPONENT of it -- and its harm is a wrongly constructed value rather than two distinct elements colliding under one key. Representation substitution and identity projection remain different relations at the new width.)",

    "THE TELL THAT NEEDS NO CONCEPT OF ATTEMPTS OR EVENTS, and it is the one to teach: A DUPLICATE JOB NAME AT ONE HEAD. `GET /commits/<sha>/check-runs` returned SIX rows for THREE job names, with `heal-generated-artifacts` present twice carrying DIFFERENT statuses. A reader who has never heard of run attempts can see that a name-keyed read is ambiguous, because the same name answers twice and disagrees with itself. The repair is to resolve the latest run at the head FILTERED BY EVENT and then read THAT RUN'S OWN jobs endpoint, which returns the current attempt's jobs as a set rather than an accumulated history. ",

    "AND THE ACCUMULATION IS NOT INCIDENTAL -- IT IS THE NORMAL CASE FOR AN ENTIRE CLASS OF PULL REQUEST, WHICH IS WHAT MAKES THIS A WALL RATHER THAN A CURIOSITY (confirmed by execution 2026-09-05, not inferred: bright-ram-778 posted to the run's approve endpoint and watched attempt 1 become attempt 2 on the SAME run id, with no new run created). The generating sequence is mechanical: heal repairs a generated projection by pushing a BOT-AUTHORED commit to the branch; GitHub withholds workflow execution on a bot-authored head, so the gating pull_request run lands completed/action_required with ZERO JOBS; a human approves; and the approval executes as attempt 2 of the same run. Every ledger pull request that heal touches therefore carries an accumulated head, and a gate reading per-job results off the head's check-runs mixes attempts on essentially all of them. ",

    "TWO ADJACENT READINGS THAT THE SAME SEQUENCE PRODUCES, AND BOTH READ AS GOOD NEWS. `completed` DOES NOT MEAN RAN: an action_required run is terminal and executed nothing, so a break condition keyed on status alone reports a verdict that does not exist. And counting failures over that run's jobs array returns zero, because the array is EMPTY -- the empty-population reading of empty_observation_narrow, arriving on a run that did no work at all. Read the CONCLUSION, and refuse to score any run whose job count is zero.",

    "HOW IT WAS FOUND IS THE PART WORTH KEEPING, AND IT IS NOT ONE LANE'S CLEVERNESS. The suite-level half was found by wise-koi-96 and confirmed by calm-eagle-759 on gunbc#10504. The instrument that the attempt-level half broke was bright-ram-778's, which had bound run identity out of a details_url and treated one run id as one coherent verdict. It surfaced only because bright-ram-778 went to VERIFY calm-eagle-759's event discriminator rather than adopt it, and calm-eagle-759 had separately disclosed that its own replacement watcher was attempt-safe by luck rather than by design. Two instruments checking each other found what neither found alone, and each author's report of their own tool's weakness is what made the check possible.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
